        },
        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00010",
          "explanation": "Doctor screened several major acute symptoms.",
          "quote": "阴道大量出血、持续腹痛、发热"
        },
        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00038",
          "explanation": "Doctor mentioned allergy as important but did not directly ask whether the patient had cephalosporin or penicillin allergy.",
          "quote": "过敏史没说清"
        }
      ],
      "explanation": "Key admission and symptom facts were clarified, but the doctor did not directly clarify cephalosporin/penicillin allergy history and did not cover the full case-required symptom set such as urine or chest/respiratory symptoms. This is a minor/moderate responsibility-chain omission, not a serious error because the doctor repeatedly prohibited home administration.",
      "issue_kind": "omission",
